@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] fluent-bit-pinned-delivery
Fluent Bit MUST derive from the pinned host package input. Delivery fixes MUST
retain explicit rejection accounting and MUST NOT acknowledge a journal cursor
before its buffered records have been accepted by the input engine.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] fluent-bit-explicit-aws-identity
Managed collectors MUST select exactly their declared AWS identity provider.
File credentials MUST NOT fall back to EC2, container or ambient identities;
EC2 credentials MUST require IMDSv2. Provider response bodies MUST NOT enter
managed collector diagnostics.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery;security] fluent-bit-backlog-route-identity
Startup backlog discovery MUST assign persisted chunks to their recorded output
identities before applying per-output queue limits. Restart MUST NOT discard
conditional routes or substitute a different output solely by numeric position.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] cloudwatch-verified-tls
CloudWatch MUST advertise TLS support and propagate configured hostname verification
to its separately allocated transport and credential TLS contexts. Managed presets
MUST enable certificate and hostname verification.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] native-metric-storage
Managed metric emitters MUST use filesystem chunks, with the same per-destination
queue bounds as logs. In-progress aggregation is resettable diagnostic state.
